│ patch_description        │ The failure was not caused by a bug in the ansatz specification or Python code. The       │
│                          │ stderr/stdout show `Evaluation error: [Errno 116] Stale file handle`, which is an         │
│                          │ OS/filesystem-level error occurring on the compute node (a1114u32n01) while the           │
│                          │ evaluation harness tried to read/write files (likely due to an NFS mount issue or a       │
│                          │ transient cluster filesystem glitch during job execution, not related to the ansatz       │
│                          │ content). Additionally the "conda: command not found" message indicates an environment    │
│                          │ activation issue in the shell init file, which is also outside the scope of the           │
│                          │ ANSATZ_SPEC file and unrelated to code correctness.                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Since ANSATZ_SPEC itself is syntactically valid, uses only allowed gates (RY, RZ, CZ)     │
│                          │ with valid wire indices (0-7), valid parameter names, and a reasonable parameter count,   │
│                          │ there is no actual bug in the circuit specification to fix. The fix here is to ensure the │
│                          │ program is self-contained, uses no external file I/O of its own, and resubmit unchanged   │
│                          │ so that the transient stale-file-handle condition (a filesystem caching issue on the      │
│                          │ cluster, unrelated to this file) does not recur. I verified the gate list, wire indices,  │
│                          │ and param strings are all valid per the schema, and kept the code structure identical to  │
│                          │ guarantee it still satisfies the fixed run_experiment interface.                          │
