                         Patch Metadata - Gen 8/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                          
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This candidate keeps the well-performing structure of the seed (per-qubit RY/RZ rotations │
│                          │ followed by nearest-neighbor entanglement) but improves connectivity and expressivity     │
│                          │ while keeping the parameter budget essentially unchanged.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes vs. the seed:                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Entanglement topology is upgraded from an open chain of CZ gates to a full **ring** of │
│                          │ CNOT gates (adds the wrap-around edge 7→0), giving every qubit at least two entangling    │
│                          │ neighbors instead of the two end qubits having only one. This increases the entangling    │
│                          │ power/depth-efficiency ratio without adding any new parameters (CNOT is unparametrized).  │
│                          │ 2. A single trainable **CRZ** gate layer is inserted along the same ring topology, with   │
│                          │ **one shared parameter** across the whole ring. This lets the circuit learn an            │
│                          │ entanglement strength (rather than being fixed at CZ-strength) while paying only 1 extra  │
│                          │ parameter for the whole block — a very parameter-efficient way to make entanglement       │
│                          │ trainable.                                                                                │
│                          │ 3. The final RZ→RZ (pre/post) double phase-rotation pattern in the seed (which is largely │
│                          │ redundant since CZ is diagonal and commutes with RZ) is replaced by a single closing RY   │
│                          │ layer, which changes basis in a way that is not redundant with the initial RY/RZ layer    │
│                          │ and should help expressivity per parameter used.                                          │
│                          │ 4. Gate count and circuit depth per block are reduced slightly relative to the seed (one  │
│                          │ fewer redundant RZ layer, one shared CRZ instead of many independent params), which       │
│                          │ should help convergence speed and reduce the train/validation gap, while the ring         │
│                          │ topology preserves/improves expressive power.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Overall this aims to: keep parameter count close to the seed's 146 (actually slightly     │
│                          │ fewer amortized per block due to sharing), improve entanglement structure (ring > chain), │
│                          │ add one cheap trainable entangling parameter, and trim redundant phase gates — targeting  │
│                          │ better validation accuracy and a smaller generalization gap while keeping/improving       │
│                          │ convergence speed.                                                                        │
