│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Building on the seed's alternating single-qubit rotation + entangling-CZ pattern, this    │
│                          │ version replaces the fixed (non-parametrized) CZ entangling layer with trainable CRZ      │
│                          │ gates arranged in a nearest-neighbor ring, and adds a second, sparser "skip-2" entangling │
│                          │ layer whose CRZ parameters are all tied together (single shared parameter). This gives    │
│                          │ the circuit tunable entanglement strength (addressing the recommendation to swap fixed CZ │
│                          │ for parametrized CRZ) while keeping the parameter count essentially unchanged versus the  │
│                          │ seed. The skip-2 connectivity (qubit i entangled with i+2 mod 8) creates longer-range     │
│                          │ correlations that a purely nearest-neighbor chain cannot capture, which should improve    │
│                          │ expressivity/accuracy, while the shared parameter on that layer acts as an implicit       │
│                          │ regularizer to curb overfitting and shrink the train/validation gap. An RX layer is       │
│                          │ inserted between the two entangling layers so that the two rotation axes (RY then RX)     │
│                          │ together with the ring CRZ realize an effectively richer single-qubit rotation before the │
│                          │ long-range mixing, without needing three separate RZ layers as in the seed.               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0492                                                                                   │
