│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ All three seed programs are identical (a linear RY→RZ‑pre→CZ‑chain→RZ‑post block), so the │
│                          │ crossover focuses on structurally improving this common ansatz rather than blending       │
│                          │ divergent designs. Two concrete architectural changes are introduced while keeping the    │
│                          │ parameter budget close to the original (146 params) so that overfitting risk stays low    │
│                          │ and reported gains are attributable to structure, not extra capacity:                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Ring closure of the entangler** – the original chain CZ(0,1)...CZ(6,7) leaves qubits │
│                          │ 0 and 7 only weakly correlated (distance 7 in the ladder). Adding a wrap‑around CZ(7,0)   │
│                          │ turns the linear chain into a ring, reducing the effective graph diameter and improving   │
│                          │ information mixing across all qubits without adding any parameters.                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **A single shared long‑range CRZ layer** – four CRZ gates connect qubits that are      │
│                          │ maximally separated in the ring (0‑4, 1‑5, 2‑6, 3‑7), all sharing **one** parameter name  │
│                          │ `"crz_shared"`. This gives the circuit direct long-range entangling capability (bypassing │
│                          │ the need for the information to propagate hop-by-hop through the ring) at the cost of     │
│                          │ just one extra trainable parameter, which is a very parameter-efficient way to boost      │
│                          │ expressivity and, empirically for such shallow HEA-style circuits, tends to reduce the    │
│                          │ train/validation gap because it lets the model capture non-local correlations directly    │
│                          │ instead of requiring deeper stacks of local gates.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The pre-entangling single-qubit stage keeps the RY→RZ ("pre") Euler-like rotation (2 free │
│                          │ angles) and the post-entangling stage keeps the single RZ per qubit, exactly mirroring    │
│                          │ the original per-qubit parameter budget (24 unique single-qubit parameters), so total     │
│                          │ added parameters are only +1 relative to the original 24 same-purpose params per block    │
│                          │ repetition (146 → ~152 total after all reps, still well within budget while giving        │
│                          │ strictly more expressive/entangling power per repetition).                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps the design simple, cheap to train, and directly targets the main weakness      │
│                          │ visible in the metrics (generalization_gap_mean 0.07, val/test accuracy noticeably below  │
│                          │ train accuracy) by improving global connectivity rather than blindly adding local         │
│                          │ parameters.                                                                               │
