│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tie_symmetric_rz_params                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Revert the extra RY-mid layer (which regressed validation accuracy to 0.85 and increased  │
│                          │ params/depth without benefit) back to the original two-RZ-layer structure, and            │
│                          │ additionally tie the pre- and post-entangler RZ parameters across symmetric qubit pairs   │
│                          │ (0↔7, 1↔6, 2↔5, 3↔4). This halves the RZ parameter count (from 16 unique RZ params to 8)  │
│                          │ while keeping the same gate count and depth, following the observation that               │
│                          │ shared-entangler parameterization previously yielded strong generalization (gap           │
│                          │ ≈0.04-0.07) and better parameter efficiency. This should recover the 0.85 score baseline  │
│                          │ while improving parameter_efficiency_mean due to fewer trainable parameters.              │
