│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tie_symmetric_rz_params                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Reduce parameter count and improve generalization by tying the pre- and post-entangling   │
│                          │ RZ rotation parameters across symmetric qubit pairs (0,7), (1,6), (2,5), (3,4). Instead   │
│                          │ of 8 independent rz_pre and 8 independent rz_post parameters, we now use only 4 shared    │
│                          │ rz_pre and 4 shared rz_post parameters, each applied to a mirror-symmetric pair of        │
│                          │ qubits. This halves the RZ parameter count (16 → 8) while preserving the same gate        │
│                          │ structure and depth, which should reduce overfitting (smaller train-test gap) similar to  │
│                          │ the gains seen with the shared long-range CRZ entangler, without sacrificing expressivity │
│                          │ since the ring topology already treats qubits symmetrically.                              │
