│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_final_ry_layer                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Add a final layer of independent RY rotations after the skip-2 CRZ entangling layer. This │
│                          │ introduces a non-commuting rotation axis after the last entangling layer, increasing      │
│                          │ expressivity of the output state without adding extra entangling depth. Prior experiments │
│                          │ show alternating RY-entangle-RY-entangle-RY patterns tend to improve both train and       │
│                          │ validation accuracy while keeping the circuit within reasonable depth (small +8 gate      │
│                          │ addition). This should help push accuracy higher; the shared-parameter skip layer already │
│                          │ limits overfitting, and we can further tune sharing if the generalization gap grows.      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
