│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ring_mixed_entangler                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current linear CZ chain (0-1,1-2,...,6-7) leaves qubits 0 and 7 disconnected and uses │
│                          │ only CZ gates uniformly. I introduce two improvements: (1) mix in CNOT gates on           │
│                          │ alternating pairs (odd-indexed links) to diversify the entangling gate set as             │
│                          │ recommended, which can help error/noise-aware optimization and break the symmetry that    │
│                          │ CZ-only layers impose; (2) close the chain into a ring by adding a CZ between qubit 7 and │
│                          │ qubit 0, giving every qubit two entangling neighbors instead of the two end qubits having │
│                          │ only one. This increases connectivity/expressivity at zero parameter cost (CZ/CNOT are    │
│                          │ fixed, non-parametrized gates) while only mildly increasing depth and gate count (one     │
│                          │ extra gate), which should improve validation accuracy and reduce the train/validation gap │
│                          │ without adding trainable parameters.                                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0228                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
