│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The previous experiment showed that the RY + alternating-shared CRZ-ring + RX +           │
│                          │ shared-skip-CRZ architecture (score 0.87) clearly outperforms the RY/RZ-sandwich design   │
│                          │ currently in the file (score 0.81). I therefore replace the current ANSATZ_SPEC with a    │
│                          │ design built on that stronger architecture, and additionally apply the recommended        │
│                          │ symmetric parameter-tying trick to the RX layer (tying `rx_i` with `rx_{7-i}`) to cut the │
│                          │ RX parameter count in half (8→4) while keeping full per-qubit RY expressivity and the     │
│                          │ proven alternating-shared CRZ ring plus single shared long-range CRZ skip connections.    │
│                          │ This keeps the well-performing entangling topology, reduces parameter count for better    │
│                          │ parameter efficiency and generalization, and should recover (and hopefully exceed) the    │
│                          │ 0.87 score while using fewer parameters than the original 0.87 design.                    │
