│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Building on the strongest prior candidate (RY → shared-pair CRZ ring → RX → single-shared │
│                          │ CRZ skip, which reached score 0.87 with only 19 unique parameters per block and fast      │
│                          │ convergence in ~180 steps), this version keeps that proven efficient core intact and      │
│                          │ appends a final per-qubit RZ layer (8 unique parameters) right before read-out. This      │
│                          │ creates the classic rotate‑entangle‑rotate‑entangle‑rotate hardware-efficient pattern:    │
│                          │ the extra terminal phase rotation gives the read-out an additional independent degree of  │
│                          │ freedom on every qubit without re-introducing the heavy per-edge parameterization that    │
│                          │ hurt the most recent (mid-RY) variant (score 0.83, 212 params, slower convergence).       │
│                          │ Parameter sharing is preserved for entangling layers (2 shared params for the ring, 1     │
│                          │ shared param for skip connections) to keep the effective parameter count and circuit      │
│                          │ depth low, aiming to improve validation accuracy and reduce the train/validation gap      │
│                          │ while remaining parameter-efficient and fast-converging.                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
