│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current version replaced the previous trainable ring entangler (CRZ) with a fixed,    │
│                          │ non-parametrized CZ ring. This removes tunable entangling strength from the               │
│                          │ nearest-neighbour connections, which likely explains the performance drop (0.81 vs        │
│                          │ 0.86-0.87 in earlier variants). Restore trainable entanglement by using CRZ gates on the  │
│                          │ ring, but keep the parameter count low by sharing a single "even" angle and a single      │
│                          │ "odd" angle across alternating ring edges (as validated in the second prior program,      │
│                          │ which achieved the highest score of 0.87). Additionally, append a final RY                │
│                          │ readout-preparation layer (one free angle per qubit) after the post-entangling RZ layer,  │
│                          │ mirroring the seed architecture's successful post-entanglement rotation layer that helps  │
│                          │ the readout observable align with the encoded correlations. This adds only 2 (ring) + 8   │
│                          │ (final RY) = 10 extra parameters while restoring meaningful entangling expressiveness and │
│                          │ improving readout flexibility.                                                            │
