│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The best-performing prior program achieved a higher score (0.87) primarily by using       │
│                          │ parameter sharing on the entangling ring (alternating even/odd shared CRZ parameters)     │
│                          │ rather than fully independent parameters, which reduced parameter count and improved      │
│                          │ generalization gap (0.06 vs 0.08). The current candidate instead uses many independent RZ │
│                          │ parameters (16 total) plus a mixed CZ/CRZ entangling layer, which increased parameter     │
│                          │ count to 212 and hurt validation/test accuracy and gap.                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit applies the same parameter-sharing philosophy to the current architecture: it   │
│                          │ replaces the 8 independent "rz_pre" and 8 independent "rz_post" single-qubit rotations    │
│                          │ with 2 shared parameters each (alternating even/odd wires), and replaces the mixed CZ+CRZ │
│                          │ entangling layer with a full 8-qubit ring of CRZ gates using two shared parameters        │
│                          │ (alternating even/odd edges, matching the proven pattern from the best prior program).    │
│                          │ This cuts total parameter count substantially (from 212 down to roughly 8+2+2+8+2 = ~40   │
│                          │ per block instance) while preserving full ring connectivity, which should reduce          │
│                          │ overfitting, shrink the train-test gap, and speed convergence, consistent with the        │
│                          │ evidence that parameter-efficient shared-rotation ansätze generalize better on this task. │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0493                                                                                   │
