│ patch_description        │ Reverting to the best-performing base structure (RY layer → alternating-strength ring CRZ │
│                          │ entangler → full RX layer → skip-2 CRZ entangler) which previously achieved the highest   │
│                          │ combined score (0.87), and additionally applying the recommended mutation: splitting the  │
│                          │ single shared `crz_skip` parameter into two alternating parameters                        │
│                          │ `crz_skip_even`/`crz_skip_odd` for the skip-2 connections. This mirrors the proven        │
│                          │ alternating-sharing pattern used successfully in the ring layer, giving the long-range    │
│                          │ entangler more expressivity (2 degrees of freedom instead of 1) while still keeping       │
│                          │ parameter count low and preserving the implicit regularization benefit of shared          │
│                          │ parameters. This should improve validation accuracy and reduce the train-test gap         │
│                          │ relative to both the fully-shared skip layer and the current CZ+long-range variant that   │
│                          │ scored lower (0.81).                                                                      │
