│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The best-performing prior ansatz (score 0.87) used *parametrized* CRZ ring entanglers     │
│                          │ (with two shared "even/odd" parameters) followed by an additional sparse skip-2 CRZ layer │
│                          │ with a single shared parameter. The current program instead uses fixed (non-trainable) CZ │
│                          │ gates for its ring entangler and has no skip-2 layer, which likely limits its ability to  │
│                          │ learn the right entangling strength and long-range correlations, contributing to its      │
│                          │ lower score (0.85) despite having more total parameters spent on local RZ layers.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit swaps the fixed CZ ring for a trainable CRZ ring (using two shared parameters   │
│                          │ "crz_ring_even"/"crz_ring_odd" to keep parameter count modest with an alternating         │
│                          │ strength pattern), keeps the existing RZ_pre/RZ_post single-qubit layers for local        │
│                          │ expressivity, and appends a lightweight skip-2 CRZ layer with one shared parameter        │
│                          │ ("crz_skip") for long-range mixing, mirroring the structure that empirically achieved the │
│                          │ best combined score. This only adds 3 extra parameters while replacing the non-trainable  │
│                          │ CZ ring with a trainable one, and should improve validation accuracy and reduce the       │
│                          │ train-test gap by letting the model learn entangling strengths rather than fixing them to │
│                          │ maximal (CZ) values.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Argumentation: Trainable ring entanglement strength was shown effective in earlier        │
│                          │ variants (CRZ ring + skip layer, score 0.87), and adding a controllable long-range skip   │
│                          │ connection increases expressivity for capturing global correlations at very low parameter │
│                          │ cost (single shared parameter), consistent with parameter-efficiency goals.               │
