╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ double_sandwich_shared_params                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Building on the best-performing seed (RY → alternating-CRZ ring → per-qubit RX → shared   │
│                          │ skip-CRZ, 116 params, score 0.87), we deepen the circuit by duplicating the entire block  │
│                          │ and appending it again while reusing the exact same parameter names (ry_0..ry_7,          │
│                          │ crz_ring_even/odd, rx_0..rx_7, crz_skip). This creates a depth-doubled, fully             │
│                          │ parameter-tied ansatz: each parameter now acts twice in the circuit (like a repeated      │
│                          │ Trotter step), increasing expressivity/entangling power without any increase in the       │
│                          │ parameter count (still 116 trainable parameters). This tests whether increased effective  │
│                          │ depth with tied weights improves representational power and generalization                │
│                          │ simultaneously, since the shared-parameter regularization already worked well for         │
│                          │ validation loss and gap in the prior run, and extra depth may help the ring/skip          │
