│ patch_name               │ add_mid_rz_layer_to_best_variant                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The best-performing prior variant (score 0.87) used: RY layer -> alternating-shared CRZ   │
│                          │ ring -> per-qubit RX layer -> single-shared-param CRZ skip layer, with ~116 params. The   │
│                          │ current program (a different, RZ/CZ-heavy variant) underperforms (0.83) with far more     │
│                          │ params (194) and a larger loss/gap. This edit reverts the EVOLVE-BLOCK to the stronger    │
│                          │ RY/CRZ-ring/RX/CRZ-skip structure and, per the recommendation, inserts a lightweight      │
│                          │ mid-circuit RZ rotation layer (one param per qubit, "rz_mid_i") between the RX layer and  │
│                          │ the skip-entanglement block. This adds a non-commuting rotation axis right before the     │
│                          │ long-range entangling layer, which should enrich the reachable state manifold and help    │
│                          │ convergence, while only adding 8 params per repetition (a modest increase, consistent     │
│                          │ with the ~+8 depth guidance) rather than the large parameter blow-up seen in the current  │
│                          │ underperforming variant.                                                                  │
