│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_diameter_entanglement                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz has strong nearest-neighbor (ring) and skip-2 entanglement but no      │
│                          │ long-range (diameter) connectivity, which may limit the model's ability to mix            │
│                          │ information globally and could contribute to the observed train-validation gap (0.08).    │
│                          │ Following the recommendation, I append a sparse diameter entanglement block: a single     │
│                          │ shared-parameter CRZ gate connecting each qubit to its antipodal partner (0-4, 1-5, 2-6,  │
│                          │ 3-7). This adds only 4 gates and 1 new trainable parameter, injecting minimal but         │
│                          │ complete long-range connectivity across the ring, which should improve                    │
│                          │ generalization/test mixing without significantly increasing parameter count, depth, or    │
│                          │ overfitting risk.                                                                         │
