│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ mixed_axis_skip_entangler                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The previous generation split the single shared skip-2 parameter into two shared          │
│                          │ parameters (crz_skip_even/odd), which increased train accuracy but widened the            │
│                          │ train-validation gap (0.08) compared to the single-parameter version (0.06 gap, higher    │
│                          │ score 0.87). This suggests the added expressivity from splitting is overfitting rather    │
│                          │ than helping generalization, and doing it homogeneously with CRZ only explores rotations  │
│                          │ around a single axis (Z).                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To recover generalization while keeping the useful long-range connectivity, I alternate   │
│                          │ the rotation axis on the skip-2 layer: keep CRZ on the even-indexed skip edges (param     │
│                          │ `crz_skip_even`) but switch the odd-indexed skip edges to CRY (new param `cry_skip_odd`). │
│                          │ This introduces axis diversity (mixing Z and Y controlled rotations) in the same sparse,  │
│                          │ parameter-shared long-range entangling layer. Axis diversity increases the Hilbert-space  │
│                          │ coverage of the entangling layer without adding new independent parameters (still just 2  │
│                          │ params for 8 gates), which should smooth the optimization landscape and potentially       │
│                          │ reduce the generalization gap while preserving or improving validation/test accuracy,     │
│                          │ consistent with the reasoning that mixing non-commuting rotation generators (Y and Z)     │
│                          │ creates richer entanglement structure than a single-axis-only approach.                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0337                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5                                                      │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 0; deleted: 0; modified: 4;                                                        │
