│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current candidate uses a fixed CZ ring (no long-range entanglement) plus pre/post RZ  │
│                          │ layers, which underperforms the earlier "crz_skip" variant that achieved 0.87 combined    │
│                          │ score. That variant used a single shared parameter for all skip-2 connections, which is   │
│                          │ very restrictive (only one trainable degree of freedom for all long-range couplings).     │
│                          │ Following the recommendation, I extend that skip-2 layer here with two alternating shared │
│                          │ parameters (`crz_skip_even` and `crz_skip_odd`), applied alternately across edges         │
│                          │ [0,2],[1,3],[2,4],[3,5],[4,6],[5,7]. This mirrors the successful ring-alternation pattern │
│                          │ already used effectively in the nearest-neighbor CRZ layers of the highest-scoring seed,  │
│                          │ giving the circuit more expressive long-range entanglement while keeping parameter count  │
│                          │ low (+2 params only) and preserving the tight regularization that keeps the               │
│                          │ generalization gap small. This should improve validation/test accuracy and reduce the     │
│                          │ loss compared to the current CZ-only long-range-free variant.                             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0301                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
