│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current candidate underperforms (score 0.83) compared to the earlier CRZ-ring +       │
│                          │ skip-2 design (score 0.87) because it replaced the trainable CRZ ring with fixed CZ gates │
│                          │ and replaced the long-range skip-2 CRZ block with a second RY rotation layer, losing the  │
│                          │ beneficial global mixing structure. This edit restores the proven CRZ-ring + RZ-pre/post  │
│                          │ + skip-2 CRZ structure from the best-performing seed, and additionally appends a          │
│                          │ single-parameter "diameter" CRZ layer connecting each qubit to its antipodal partner      │
│                          │ (0-4, 1-5, 2-6, 3-7). This adds long-range (distance-4) entanglement using only one extra │
│                          │ trainable parameter, which should improve global feature mixing and generalization        │
│                          │ (reducing train-test gap) without significantly increasing parameter count or depth,      │
│                          │ consistent with the sparse/shared-parameter regularization strategy that worked well      │
│                          │ previously.                                                                               │
