│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ duplicate_shared_ring_block                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The two prior seed variants that reached the best score (0.87) both used an RY encoding   │
│                          │ layer followed by a nearest-neighbor CRZ ring with shared alternating parameters, then an │
│                          │ entangling/rotation combo (RX + skip/diameter CRZ layers). The current candidate (CZ-only │
│                          │ entangler with unshared RY/RZ pre/post layers) underperforms (0.83) and has more          │
│                          │ parameters (194) than needed.                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I revert to the higher-scoring architecture (RY -> CRZ ring with shared even/odd params   │
│                          │ -> symmetric-tied RX -> shared skip-2 CRZ -> shared diameter CRZ), and then duplicate     │
│                          │ that entire block a second time while reusing exactly the same parameter names. This      │
│                          │ doubles the effective circuit depth (more entangling layers -> higher expressivity)       │
│                          │ without increasing the parameter count at all, testing whether extra tied-parameter depth │
│                          │ improves accuracy/generalization further, consistent with the recommendation to stack a   │
│                          │ shared-parameter "sandwich".                                                              │
