│ patch_description        │ Builds on the best-performing seed (RY layer + alternating shared-parameter CRZ ring +    │
│                          │ symmetrically-tied RX layer + shared-parameter skip/diameter entanglers), which achieved  │
│                          │ a strong 0.87 score with efficient parameter usage. Following the recommendation, I       │
│                          │ insert a lightweight mid-circuit RZ rotation layer between the RX layer and the           │
│                          │ skip/diameter entangling block. This RZ layer is tied with the same left-right mirror     │
│                          │ symmetry used for the RX layer (rz_mid_0=rz_mid_7, rz_mid_1=rz_mid_6, rz_mid_2=rz_mid_5,  │
│                          │ rz_mid_3=rz_mid_4), adding only 4 new parameters and 8 gates. This enriches local phase   │
│                          │ control right before the long-range entanglers fire, giving the circuit an extra degree   │
│                          │ of freedom to shape the state's relative phases in a symmetric, regularized way that      │
│                          │ mirrors the RX layer's inductive bias, without significantly increasing parameter count   │
│                          │ or depth. The ring entangler keeps the alternating-parameter CRZ scheme (2 params for 8   │
│                          │ gates) which was shown to work well, and the skip-2 / diameter layers keep single shared  │
│                          │ parameters for cheap long-range mixing.                                                   │
