│ patch_name               │ mixed_axis_skip_entanglement                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Building on the best-performing prior architecture (RY → ring-CRZ → RX → skip-CRZ,        │
│                          │ duplicated with shared params, score 0.89), this edit diversifies the skip-2 entangling   │
│                          │ layer by splitting it into two interleaved sub-layers that use different rotation axes:   │
│                          │ CRZ on the "even" skip edges and CRY on the "odd" skip edges, each with their own shared  │
│                          │ parameter (crz_skip_even / cry_skip_odd). This mirrors the successful even/odd            │
│                          │ shared-parameter pattern already used in the ring layer, but now mixes Z- and Y-axis      │
│                          │ controlled rotations to diversify the entangling interactions without adding depth or     │
│                          │ many extra parameters (only one additional parameter total). Diversifying interaction     │
│                          │ axes tends to smooth the optimization landscape and can improve                           │
│                          │ expressivity/generalization, as hypothesized in the recommendation. The whole block is    │
│                          │ duplicated (reusing the same parameter names) to double effective depth while keeping     │
│                          │ parameter count low, following the pattern that gave the best score (0.89) previously.    │
