│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the two best-performing seed variants (both scoring 0.89) that combined      │
│                          │ RY→ring-CRZ→RX→skip-CRZ layers, duplicated into two shared-parameter blocks. The first    │
│                          │ variant added a two-parameter "diameter" (antipodal) CRZ layer for global mixing and      │
│                          │ achieved a smaller train/val gap (0.03) but slower convergence (540 steps); the second    │
│                          │ omitted the diameter layer and converged much faster (150 steps) at the cost of a larger  │
│                          │ gap (0.06).                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version keeps the fast-converging modular block structure (RY, alternating-shared    │
│                          │ ring-CRZ, RX, single-shared skip-2 CRZ) and adds a *minimal* global entangler: a diameter │
│                          │ (antipodal, distance-4) CRZ layer that uses a **single** shared parameter instead of two. │
│                          │ This keeps the extra global-mixing benefit (which improved generalization gap in variant  │
│                          │ 1) while adding only one extra trainable parameter instead of two, keeping the parameter  │
│                          │ count low (20 unique parameters) and reusing the same names across both stacked block     │
│                          │ copies to preserve the fast convergence properties from variant 2. The result should      │
│                          │ combine the best of both: faster convergence, low parameter count (better parameter       │
│                          │ efficiency), and improved generalization from the added global connectivity.              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0549                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
