                         Patch Metadata - Gen 56/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_mirrored_rz_mid_layer                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Insert a lightweight mid-circuit RZ rotation layer between the RX rotations (Layer 3) and │
│                          │ the skip/diameter entangling blocks. The RZ parameters are tied in mirror pairs across    │
│                          │ the qubit register (wire 0 with wire 7, wire 1 with wire 6, etc.), so only 4 unique       │
│                          │ parameters are added regardless of qubit count. This introduces structured phase control  │
│                          │ that can sharpen local expressivity (by giving each qubit an extra rotation axis right    │
│                          │ before the longer-range entangling gates) while keeping the parameter count essentially   │
│                          │ unchanged, since the mirror-sharing trick reuses the "shared depth" regularization idea   │
│                          │ that has previously improved generalization gap and test accuracy in this ansatz family.  │
│                          │ The expectation is a modest boost in validation/test accuracy and possibly faster         │
│                          │ convergence, without the parameter-count blow-up that a fully independent RZ layer would  │
│                          │ cause.                                                                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0282                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5                                                      │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 16; deleted: 0; modified: 0;                                                       │
