│                          │ optimization landscape (likely mild barren-plateau-like gradient degradation from the     │
│                          │ added long-range diameter entanglers stacked twice). Since parameter count is unchanged   │
│                          │ by duplication (parameters are shared), the doubling only adds depth/gates without adding │
│                          │ capacity — a pure cost with apparently diminishing accuracy return and a large            │
│                          │ convergence-speed penalty.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit applies the (already-improved) single block, containing RY rotations, ring CRZ, │
│                          │ RX rotations, skip-2 CRZ, and the new diameter CRZ layer, exactly once instead of twice.  │
│                          │ This keeps the newly added global diameter-entanglement structure while cutting           │
│                          │ depth/gate-count roughly in half, which should substantially speed up convergence and     │
│                          │ reduce the risk of vanishing gradients from excessive depth, while retaining the same     │
│                          │ parameter count (since sharing already made duplication "free" in parameters) and the     │
│                          │ same expressive layer types per block.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ If validation/test accuracy drop too much from having only one pass, a natural follow-up  │
│                          │ would be to re-introduce a partial second pass (e.g., only the entangling layers) rather  │
│                          │ than the full block, but as a first targeted step we test the depth-halving change in     │
│                          │ isolation to isolate its effect on convergence speed and generalization gap.              │
