│                          │ diameter-CRZ, block reused twice with shared params) by inserting a lightweight,          │
│                          │ mirror-paired RZ phase layer between the RX rotation layer and the skip-2 entangler. The  │
│                          │ four new shared parameters (`rz_mid_0..3`) couple antipodal-ish qubit pairs (0&7, 1&6,    │
│                          │ 2&5, 3&4) via same-parameter RZ rotations, injecting a cheap global phase-correlation     │
│                          │ signal right where local (RX) and mid-range (skip) information mix. This is expected to   │
│                          │ sharpen local expressivity and speed convergence (as seen in the skip-2 variant's fast    │
│                          │ 150-step convergence) while retaining the diameter-CRZ global mixing and block-level      │
│                          │ parameter sharing that gave the modular design its best generalization gap (0.03) and     │
│                          │ combined score (0.89). Net cost is only +4 parameters over the strongest prior modular    │
│                          │ design.                                                                                   │
