│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ mixed_axis_ring_entangler                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Enhance two-qubit axis diversity in the ring entangler layer: currently all ring edges    │
│                          │ use CRZ with alternating shared parameters (crz_ring_even/crz_ring_odd). We change the    │
│                          │ odd edges to use CRY instead of CRZ, keeping crz_ring_even on even edges and introducing  │
│                          │ cry_ring_odd on odd edges. Mixing rotation axes (Z and Y) in the entangling layer         │
│                          │ increases the expressivity of the circuit's effective unitary group coverage without      │
│                          │ adding any extra gates, depth, or parameters (same count, just relabeled param name and   │
│                          │ gate type). This mirrors the successful skip-2/skip-3 mixed-axis pattern already used     │
│                          │ elsewhere in the ansatz (CRZ/CRY alternation), and prior generations (seed variant 2)     │
│                          │ showed accuracy gains from axis mixing in the skip-connections; applying the same         │
│                          │ principle to the ring layer should further improve expressivity and validation accuracy   │
│                          │ at zero extra cost.                                                                       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
