│ patch_name               │ diameter_alternating_split                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the single shared "crz_diam" parameter in `_diameter_crz` with two alternating    │
│                          │ parameters (`crz_diam_even` for pairs [0,4] and [2,6], `crz_diam_odd` for pairs [1,5] and │
│                          │ [3,7]). This mirrors the alternating-strength motif already used successfully in the ring │
│                          │ entanglement layer (Gen35/Gen38 lineage), giving the global antipodal connections         │
│                          │ slightly more expressive freedom (2 params instead of 1) while still keeping parameter    │
│                          │ count low and preserving the shared-parameter regularization benefit. This should improve │
│                          │ mixing/expressivity for global correlations without meaningfully increasing parameter     │
│                          │ count or depth.                                                                           │
