│ patch_description        │ Revert to the higher-scoring modular block design (RY -> ring CRZ -> RX -> skip-2 CRZ ->  │
│                          │ skip-3 CRZ -> diameter CRZ) that previously achieved test_accuracy 0.90 / score 0.89,     │
│                          │ replacing the current simpler block (which regressed to 0.87). Additionally extend from   │
│                          │ two stacked copies to three stacked copies of the same shared-parameter block, testing    │
│                          │ whether extra shared depth (without increasing parameter count) yields further accuracy   │
│                          │ gains, per the recommendation. Parameter count stays fixed since all copies reuse         │
│                          │ identical parameter names; only depth/gate-count increase, which should improve           │
│                          │ expressivity while the strong parameter sharing continues to act as an implicit           │
│                          │ regularizer, keeping the train-validation gap controlled.                                 │
