│ patch_description        │ The current candidate (single ring + skip-2 + diamond-CRX, doubled) regressed to 0.87,    │
│                          │ while the earlier modular version with ry/rx layers, ring-CRZ, skip-2, skip-3, and        │
│                          │ diameter-CRZ entanglement (doubled) achieved the best score so far (0.89) with good test  │
│                          │ accuracy (0.90) and lower loss. I restore that better-performing modular block structure, │
│                          │ and per the recommendation, extend it to three repetitions (all sharing identical         │
│                          │ parameter names) instead of two. This increases circuit depth/expressivity without adding │
│                          │ any new parameters, testing whether additional shared-parameter depth further improves    │
│                          │ generalization beyond the 2-block version, while keeping the same low parameter count     │
│                          │ (128) that already showed strong results.                                                 │
