│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The best-performing prior generation (score 0.89, lowest test loss/gap) used a modular    │
│                          │ layer structure with skip-2, skip-3 and diameter entangling layers. The current program   │
│                          │ regressed to a simpler, less effective topology (single skip-2 layer + distance-4 CRX)    │
│                          │ and dropped the skip-3 layer entirely, hurting both convergence speed and generalization  │
│                          │ (0.87 score, convergence_step jumped to 540). This edit restores the modular              │
│                          │ skip-2/skip-3/diameter architecture from the best generation, and additionally implements │
│                          │ the recommended improvement: splitting each skip-2 and skip-3 entangling layer into two   │
│                          │ alternating shared parameters (even/odd indexed edges) rather than a single shared        │
│                          │ parameter per layer. This mirrors the proven alternating-strength pattern already used    │
│                          │ successfully in the nearest-neighbor ring layer, giving the mid-range entanglers slightly │
│                          │ more expressive freedom (two knobs instead of one) while still keeping parameter count    │
│                          │ low via sharing. The expectation is tighter long-range mixing, reduced train-test gap,    │
│                          │ and faster convergence, consistent with the ring layer's alternating design that has      │
│                          │ repeatedly performed well.                                                                │
