                         Patch Metadata - Gen 68/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the modular, well-documented block-construction style of the      │
│                          │ second seed (which achieved the best test accuracy 0.90 and lowest validation/test loss   │
│                          │ thanks to its rich set of entanglers: nearest-neighbor ring, skip-2, skip-3 and diameter  │
│                          │ connections) with the entangling-gate diversity of the first seed (which alternated CRZ   │
│                          │ and CRY on its skip-connections, giving richer non-commuting mixing at the same parameter │
│                          │ cost).                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key design choices:                                                                       │
│                          │ 1. Per-qubit RY then RX rotation layers give full single-qubit expressivity (16           │
│                          │ params/block).                                                                            │
│                          │ 2. A nearest-neighbor ring of CRZ gates with two alternating shared parameters gives      │
│                          │ local entanglement at minimal parameter cost (2 params/block), as in both seeds.          │
│                          │ 3. The skip-2 entangling layer now alternates CRZ and CRY (instead of being purely CRZ as │
│                          │ in the second seed), directly reusing the winning idea from the first seed that mixing    │
│                          │ rotation axes on the entangling gates increases expressivity without adding parameters (2 │
│                          │ params/block).                                                                            │
│                          │ 4. A skip-3 layer (single shared CRZ parameter) fills in the previously-missing           │
│                          │ distance-3 connectivity, as introduced in the second seed.                                │
│                          │ 5. A diameter (distance N/2) CRZ layer gives one global, all-to-half-way connection with  │
│                          │ a single shared parameter, providing long-range mixing cheaply.                           │
│                          │ 6. The whole block is applied twice with identical parameter names (weight-tying across   │
│                          │ depth), doubling the effective circuit depth/expressivity while keeping the parameter     │
│                          │ count fixed — the same "shared-depth" trick that drove the accuracy gains in both seeds.  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This gives only 22 unique parameters (11 rotation/skip families x 2 not counted correctly │
│                          │ — actually 8 RY + 2 ring + 8 RX + 2 skip2 + 1 skip3 + 1 diam = 22), a large reduction     │
│                          │ versus the 122-146 params of the seeds, which should improve parameter efficiency and     │
│                          │ convergence speed while retaining the entangling richness (ring + skip2 + skip3 +         │
│                          │ diameter, mixed CRZ/CRY) that produced the strongest validation/test performance in the   │
