│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Reverting to the modular ansatz structure from the best-performing prior program (score   │
│                          │ 0.89, 128 params) and applying the recommended refinement: instead of a single shared     │
│                          │ parameter for all skip-2 edges and all skip-3 edges, alternate between two shared         │
│                          │ parameters (even/odd indexed edges) for each skip distance. This mirrors the proven       │
│                          │ alternating-strength motif already used successfully in the ring layer, giving            │
│                          │ finer-grained control over long-range entanglement strength while only adding 2 extra     │
│                          │ parameters (4 total instead of 2 for skip layers). This should tighten mid-range mixing   │
│                          │ and potentially reduce the generalization gap while keeping parameter count modest (132   │
│                          │ vs 128).                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current file (with rz_pre/rz_post ansatz, 176 params, score 0.86) is replaced         │
│                          │ wholesale with the better modular structure plus this refinement.                         │
