│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz applies a fixed sequence of layers (RY, ring-CRZ, RX, skip-CRZ/CRY)    │
│                          │ exactly twice, sharing all parameter names between the two copies. Based on the           │
│                          │ recommendation to test whether additional shared-depth repetition improves performance    │
│                          │ without increasing parameter count, I add a third identical copy of the block (again      │
│                          │ reusing the same parameter names). This increases circuit depth/expressivity (more        │
│                          │ entangling layers to build up correlations) while keeping n_params unchanged at 122,      │
│                          │ testing whether the added depth pushes validation accuracy and combined score higher,     │
│                          │ similar to the depth-doubling effect observed between the first (0.87) and second (0.89)  │
│                          │ prior programs.                                                                           │
