│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_third_shared_block                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Extend the shared-parameter "shared depth" trick one step further by applying the ansatz  │
│                          │ block three times instead of two, reusing the same parameter names across all three       │
│                          │ copies. This increases circuit depth/expressivity (more entangling layers to mix          │
│                          │ information across qubits) while keeping the parameter count fixed at 128, testing        │
│                          │ whether the previous scaling trend (0.78 -> 0.89 when going from 1 to 2 blocks) continues │
│                          │ to yield gains in validation accuracy and loss reduction without hurting convergence      │
│                          │ speed too much. Since deeper circuits with shared parameters acted as an effective        │
│                          │ regularizer in prior generations (reducing train-test gap), a third repetition may        │
│                          │ further close the generalization gap and improve test performance, though we monitor      │
│                          │ convergence_step to ensure training still converges efficiently.                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
