│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current program's flat, single-block ansatz underperforms (score 0.85) compared to    │
│                          │ the earlier modular two-block design (score 0.89) that used per-qubit RY/RX layers, a     │
│                          │ ring CRZ layer with alternating even/odd shared parameters, skip-2/skip-3 CRZ layers, and │
│                          │ a diameter CRZ layer, all repeated twice for depth without doubling parameters. I'm       │
│                          │ reverting to that stronger modular structure and additionally applying the recommended    │
│                          │ refinement: split the skip-2 and skip-3 entanglers into alternating even/odd shared       │
│                          │ parameters (analogous to the successful ring layer's even/odd split), rather than a       │
│                          │ single shared parameter per skip distance. This should tighten mid-range entanglement     │
│                          │ expressivity at the cost of only +2 parameters, likely improving validation accuracy and  │
│                          │ shrinking the generalization gap below the prior 0.06.                                    │
