│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current candidate (plain RY-RZ-CZ-RY-RZ ansatz) scores only 0.83, clearly worse than  │
│                          │ the modular, skip-connected, shared-parameter architecture that previously achieved 0.89  │
│                          │ combined score with better generalization gap and loss. I restore that stronger modular   │
│                          │ architecture (per-qubit RY, ring CRZ, per-qubit RX, skip-2/skip-3/diameter CRZ            │
│                          │ entanglers, block repeated twice with shared params) and additionally insert the          │
│                          │ recommended mirror-paired RZ phase layer between the RX layer and the skip-2 entangler.   │
│                          │ The mirror RZ layer applies RZ to antipodal-ish pairs (0&7, 1&6, 2&5, 3&4) sharing 4      │
│                          │ parameters, adding symmetric local phase control that should sharpen expressivity and     │
│                          │ help convergence without inflating parameter count much (+4 params per block usage, but   │
│                          │ since params are shared by name across both block copies, total added params stay at 4).  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Argumentation: The modular architecture already demonstrated the best combined score      │
│                          │ (0.89) with lower validation/test loss than the seed's flat approach. Adding a            │
│                          │ lightweight symmetric phase layer targeting qubit pairs symmetric about the center is a   │
│                          │ natural way to inject additional local nonlinearity in phase space, which especially      │
│                          │ helps RZ/CRZ-heavy circuits where phase information otherwise gets underused. Placing it  │
│                          │ right after the RX layer (second rotation axis) and before skip-2 entanglement (mid-range │
│                          │ mixing) means the phases get entangled into the ring/skip/diameter structure fully, per   │
│                          │ the recommendation.                                                                       │
