╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover merges the clean, modular layer-construction style of the second seed      │
│                          │ (functions for RY/RX layers, ring entanglement, skip entanglement, diameter entanglement) │
│                          │ with the axis-diversified skip-connection trick from the current program (alternating     │
│                          │ CRZ/CRY on the skip-2 layer instead of a single-axis CRZ). The skip-3 layer from the pure │
│                          │ modular version is dropped to cut gate count/depth (which should help convergence speed,  │
│                          │ similar to the current program's faster convergence at step 150) while keeping the        │
│                          │ single-parameter antipodal "diameter" CRZ layer for cheap global mixing (which            │
│                          │ contributed to the modular version's better validation/test loss of 0.31/0.34). The block │
│                          │ is still duplicated with fully shared parameter names to double effective depth without   │
│                          │ inflating the parameter count, following the pattern that worked well in both parents.    │
│                          │ This combination aims to capture the best of both: fast convergence, low generalization   │
│                          │ gap, and strong validation/test loss with an efficient parameter budget.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Concretely, one block is:                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. RY layer (8 independent params) — expressivity.                                        │
│                          │ 2. Ring CRZ, alternating shared params (2 params) — local nearest-neighbor mixing.        │
│                          │ 3. RX layer (8 independent params) — second rotation axis.                                │
│                          │ 4. Skip-2 entanglement alternating CRZ/CRY (2 params) — mid-range mixing with axis        │
│                          │ diversity, cheaper and more expressive than a single-axis skip layer.                     │
│                          │ 5. Diameter (distance-4) CRZ, single shared param — cheap global mixing across the whole  │
│                          │ register.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This block is applied twice with fully shared parameter names, giving depth without added │
│                          │ parameter cost.                                                                           │
