│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current seed (RY+RZ+CZ-ring+RZ) underperforms (0.85) compared to the best prior       │
│                          │ program (0.89) which used modular RY/RX rotation layers combined with ring, skip-2,       │
│                          │ skip-3, and diameter CRZ entanglers repeated across two blocks with shared parameters. I  │
│                          │ restore that stronger modular architecture and additionally insert a single-parameter     │
│                          │ "star" CRZ layer (hub qubit 0 connected via CRZ to every other qubit) after the diameter  │
│                          │ layer in each block. This hub-and-spoke entangler adds global connectivity complementary  │
│                          │ to the ring/skip/diameter distances at the cost of only one extra shared parameter, which │
│                          │ prior evidence suggests strengthens generalization without much added depth or parameter  │
│                          │ overhead. Reusing the same "crz_star" parameter across both block copies keeps parameter  │
│                          │ count low while doubling the depth of this new global-mixing layer.                       │
